info.studentTasks:
(1) read and understand rightly all relevant documents for the CPs published on FLM (such as guidelines, requirements, and regulations, etc.);

(2) Participate in the Orientation meeting conducted by the Department

(3) Choose topics for Capstone Projects so that the topics fall within the concentrations, and fully meet the requirements of common research ethics, law, fine customs and traditional values in Vietnam; an approval from supervisor(s) and the University may be required.

(3) Divide and schedule work for each member of group approximatelly based on supervisor(s)' advise and the CP Guidelines and Syllabus;

(4) Students are required to attend at least 80% of scheduled meetings with their supervisor(s) to be eligible for the thesis or capstone defense;

(5) Conduct research, produce documents and media products, and write reports (in English) according to the CPs requirements from the University and the Department; preference the Guideline for details.

(6) Avoiding Plagiarism and Copyright Infringement in all reports and media productions;

(7) Defense individually the CPs in front of examination Committees according to the requirements and regulations of the University and the Department.

